# Global gitignore for this domain — deploys to ~/.gitignore_global (the base's
# core.excludesfile points here). Overlay-owned because git reads exactly one global ignore
# file, so a domain's additions and the defaults have to live in the same one.
#
# THE LINES ABOVE THE MARKER ARE THE BASE'S DEFAULTS, and overlay-doctor fails an overlay whose
# ~/.gitignore_global lacks any of them (this file is its list). Keep them; APPEND your domain's
# own ignores below the marker.
.exrc
.envrc

# AI agent state: per-user and per-machine, never a project's to carry. Enumerated by filename
# rather than a `*.local.*` glob, which would also swallow unrelated project files. The test: would
# this file be wrong on another machine, or for another person? Per-user permission grants and
# harness-created worktrees are; shared agent context (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md,
# .claude/settings.json, authored project skills) is committed instead.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.local.md
**/.claude/.cc-writes/
# A parked session's relaunch script, rewritten at every park (ignored by exact name, since
# .claude/ itself carries tracked files in many repos).
.claude/canonical-kickoff.sh
# Worktrunk's worktrees for an ordinary (non-bare) checkout, which nest inside the repo.
.worktrees/
# --- domain-specific additions below ---
